author ai
group features/gui
note Ctrl-click or double-click an identifier in any code view (document, listing, peek, graph node) to go to its definition. A definition that is a symbol in the repo lands on that symbol: the matching step of the path being read when there is one, otherwise the Listing. A definition inside a symbol (a field, a local) opens the Listing on its line. One outside the repo cannot be jumped to and is shown in the peek panel instead, with a status line saying where it is. With a language server the answer arrives a few frames later; without one, the symbol of that name is used; prose files do nothing. No definition found is reported in the status bar.

